{"type":"message","id":"31ee21dd","parentId":"9b9f076d","timestamp":"2026-01-30T21:14:36.211Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Write a 2-page concept note for the Biomed BorBor project — a WhatsApp-based biomedical equipment troubleshooting bot for technicians in Sierra Leone and Liberia.\n\nContext:\n- Project path: /home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/medtech-bot/\n- Read existing files there for context on the knowledge base and architecture\n- WhatsApp Business registered, 6 equipment types, 399 troubleshooting nodes, Krio + Liberian English support\n- Target funders: Grand Challenges, USAID DIV, PIH (Partners in Health)\n- Doug has biomedical engineering background and PIH context\n- Key technical innovation to highlight: **adversarial multi-agent safety architecture** inspired by the paper \"If You Want Coherence, Orchestrate a Team of Rivals\" (arxiv 2601.14351)\n  - Triage agent understands the problem\n  - Diagnostic agent walks troubleshooting trees\n  - Safety critic agent vetoes dangerous recommendations\n  - This means reliability through organizational structure, not just a smarter model\n\nWrite the concept note to /home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/medtech-bot/CONCEPT-NOTE.md\n\nStructure:\n1. **Problem Statement** — Equipment downtime in low-resource health facilities, lack of on-site biomed expertise, language barriers\n2. **Proposed Solution** — Biomed BorBor: WhatsApp-native troubleshooting assistant with multi-agent safety architecture\n3. **Technical Innovation** — Adversarial agent architecture ensuring safety-critical reliability without human fallback\n4. **Target Users & Context** — Biomed techs, nurses, facility managers in Sierra Leone/Liberia (PIH network)\n5. **Implementation Plan** — Phased rollout, equipment coverage, language support, feedback loops\n6. **Budget Estimate** — Ballpark for pilot phase (WhatsApp API, compute, local partnerships)\n7. **Team & Partners** — Doug's background, PIH relationship, technical capacity\n\nTone: Compelling but grounded. Funder-ready. Not hype — real problem, real solution, real innovation. Keep it to 2 pages (roughly 800-1000 words)."}],"timestamp":1769807676210}}
