{"type":"message","id":"096824bb","parentId":"c5985079","timestamp":"2026-01-30T21:14:44.221Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01CE63ogGoKs6pTtdyYv4fZ3","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/medtech-bot/README.md"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01UEPtc5kKk3zQ62anLFxkAQ","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/medtech-bot/src/services/conversationEngine.js","limit":50}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01UZmETFfqJsDSCqSiBQ2skE","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cat /home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/medtech-bot/data/troubleshooting-trees/oxygen_concentrator.json | python3 -c \"import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(f'Nodes: {len(d.get(\\\"nodes\\\",d.get(\\\"tree\\\",[])))}')\" 2>/dev/null; for f in /home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/medtech-bot/data/troubleshooting-trees/*.json; do echo -n \"$(basename $f): \"; python3 -c \"import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin); keys=list(d.keys()); print(keys[:5])\" < \"$f\" 2>/dev/null; done"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-opus-4-5","usage":{"input":1,"output":367,"cacheRead":10033,"cacheWrite":1152,"totalTokens":11553,"cost":{"input":0.000005,"output":0.009175,"cacheRead":0.0050165,"cacheWrite":0.007200000000000001,"total":0.021396500000000002}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1769807679002}}
{"type":"message","id":"98334148","parentId":"096824bb","timestamp":"2026-01-30T21:14:44.231Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01CE63ogGoKs6pTtdyYv4fZ3","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# MedTech Bot 🏥\n\nWhatsApp bot for biomedical equipment technicians in low-resource health facilities (Sierra Leone/Liberia, PIH context).\n\n## What it does\n\n- Walks technicians through **troubleshooting decision trees** conversationally via WhatsApp\n- **Logs every issue**: equipment type, model, facility, failure description, steps taken, resolution, time to resolve, parts needed\n- **Cross-facility learning**: when a tech resolves an issue, the resolution is stored and surfaced to other techs facing similar problems\n\n## Supported Equipment\n\n| Equipment | Common Issues Covered |\n|---|---|\n| **Oxygen Concentrators** (DeVilbiss, AirSep, Longfian) | Low flow, overheating, sieve bed, compressor, power, alarms, noise |\n| **Patient Monitors** (Edan iM50/60) | Display, SpO2, ECG, NIBP, temperature probe, battery, alarms |\n| **Infant Incubators** (Phoenix, David) | Temperature regulation, humidity, fan failure, alarms, power |\n\n## Setup\n\n### 1. Install dependencies\n\n```bash\nnpm install\n```\n\n### 2. Configure environment\n\n```bash\ncp .env.example .env\n# Edit .env with your WhatsApp Cloud API credentials\n```\n\n### 3. Initialize database\n\n```bash\nnpm run migrate\nnpm run seed\n```\n\n### 4. Run\n\n```bash\nnpm start        # Production\nnpm run dev      # Development (auto-reload)\n```\n\n### 5. Configure WhatsApp webhook\n\nSet your Meta App webhook URL to:\n```\nhttps://your-domain.com/webhook\n```\n\nVerification token must match `WHATSAPP_VERIFY_TOKEN` in `.env`.\n\n## Docker\n\n```bash\ndocker build -t medtech-bot .\ndocker run -p 3000:3000 --env-file .env medtech-bot\n```\n\n## Project Structure\n\n```\nmedtech-bot/\n├── src/\n│   ├── index.js                    # Express server entry\n│   ├── routes/\n│   │   ├── webhook.js              # WhatsApp webhook (GET verify + POST messages)\n│   │   └── health.js               # Health check endpoint\n│   ├── services/\n│   │   ├── conversationEngine.js   # State machine managing dialogues\n│   │   ├── troubleshootingTrees.js # Loads and navigates JSON decision trees\n│   │   ├── crossFacilityLearning.js # Resolution storage and similarity matching\n│   │   └── whatsapp.js             # WhatsApp Cloud API client\n│   └── models/\n│       └── db.js                   # SQLite database initialization\n├── data/\n│   └── troubleshooting-trees/      # Editable JSON decision trees\n│       ├── oxygen_concentrator.json\n│       ├── patient_monitor.json\n│       └── infant_incubator.json\n├── migrations/\n│   ├── run.js                      # Database schema migration\n│   └── seed.js                     # Seed data (facilities, equipment)\n├── package.json\n├── Dockerfile\n├── .env.example\n└── README.md\n```\n\n## Conversation Flow\n\n1. Tech sends \"hi\" → Bot asks for name (first time only)\n2. Bot shows equipment menu\n3. Tech selects equipment type → brand\n4. Bot walks through troubleshooting tree step by step\n5. At each node: question → tech responds → next step\n6. Resolution found → issue logged with parts needed, time taken\n7. Resolution stored for cross-facility learning\n\n## Editing Troubleshooting Trees\n\nTrees are JSON files in `data/troubleshooting-trees/`. Each node has:\n\n- `type`: `menu` | `question` | `resolution` | `info` | `input` | `end` | `system`\n- `text`: Message shown to the technician\n- `options`: Map of user response → next node ID\n- `parts`: Array of parts that may be needed (optional)\n- `escalate`: Boolean flag for issues needing escalation (optional)\n\nAdd new trees by creating a JSON file with the same structure and an `id` field.\n\n## API Endpoints\n\n- `GET /health` — Health check with stats\n- `GET /webhook` — WhatsApp webhook verification\n- `POST /webhook` — Incoming WhatsApp messages\n\n## Data Model\n\n- **technicians** — phone, name, facility\n- **facilities** — name, location, country, district\n- **equipment** — type, brand, model, serial, facility\n- **issues** — full issue lifecycle with timing\n- **issue_steps** — each troubleshooting step taken\n- **resolutions** — cross-facility learning store\n- **conversations** — current conversation state per phone number\n\n## License\n\nMIT\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1769807684230}}
{"type":"message","id":"ba5be482","parentId":"98334148","timestamp":"2026-01-30T21:14:44.237Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01UEPtc5kKk3zQ62anLFxkAQ","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"const { v4: uuidv4 } = require('uuid');\nconst { getDb } = require('../models/db');\nconst { getTree, getAllTrees, getNode, matchOption, formatNodeWithOptions } = require('./troubleshootingTrees');\nconst { storeResolution, findSimilarResolutions, formatSimilarResolutions } = require('./crossFacilityLearning');\nconst { t } = require('../i18n/strings');\nconst { downloadWhatsAppMedia } = require('./whatsapp');\nconst path = require('path');\nconst fs = require('fs');\n\n// Aliases for fuzzy equipment matching\nconst EQUIPMENT_ALIASES = {\n  'oxygen_concentrator': ['oxygen', 'o2', 'o2 concentrator', 'concentrator', 'ox con'],\n  'infant_incubator': ['incubator', 'infant', 'baby warmer', 'warmer', 'nicu'],\n  'patient_monitor': ['monitor', 'patient monitor', 'vital signs', 'vitals', 'edan', 'pulse ox', 'spo2'],\n  'autoclave': ['autoclave', 'sterilizer', 'steriliser', 'steam sterilizer', 'tuttnauer', 'prestige', 'cssd'],\n  'centrifuge': ['centrifuge', 'spinner', 'hematocrit', 'blood spinner', 'lab centrifuge', '80-2', 'hettich'],\n  'suction_machine': ['suction', 'suction machine', 'suction pump', 'aspirator', 'vacuum suction', 'medela', 'laerdal', 'yankauer'],\n};\n\n// Fuzzy match: returns index (0-based) into treeIds or -1\nfunction fuzzyMatchEquipment(input, treeIds) {\n  const norm = input.trim().toLowerCase();\n  for (let i = 0; i < treeIds.length; i++) {\n    const treeId = treeIds[i];\n    const tree = getTree(treeId);\n    if (tree.name.toLowerCase().includes(norm) || norm.includes(tree.name.toLowerCase())) return i;\n    const aliases = EQUIPMENT_ALIASES[treeId] || [];\n    for (const alias of aliases) {\n      if (norm.includes(alias) || alias.includes(norm)) return i;\n    }\n  }\n  return -1;\n}\n\n// Fuzzy match brand name against list\nfunction fuzzyMatchBrand(input, brands) {\n  const norm = input.trim().toLowerCase();\n  for (let i = 0; i < brands.length; i++) {\n    const brand = brands[i].toLowerCase();\n    if (brand.includes(norm) || norm.includes(brand)) return i;\n    const words = norm.split(/\\s+/);\n    if (words.some(w => w.length > 2 && brand.includes(w))) return i;\n  }\n  return -1;\n}\n\n// Get or create conversation state\nfunction getConversation(phone) {\n  const db = getDb();\n  let conv = db.prepare('SELECT * FROM conversations WHERE phone = ?').get(phone);\n\n[580 more lines in file. Use offset=51 to continue]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1769807684233}}
